{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":34,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.heckeH_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.heckeH_pos","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L247-L252","doc":"`h = q - q⁻¹ > 0` for `q > 1`: the hypothesis the substrate supplies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.L_strict_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.L_strict_mono","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L235-L245","doc":"**`L_pp < L_pn < L_nn`, for every `q > 0` and every `δ ∈ (0,2)`.** The bound\ntwo-body system is assigned the MIDDLE bond constant, and no choice of `q` changes it:\n`L = -log(z + d)` is strictly decreasing in the offset, and the `pn` offset is a convex\ncombination of the other two. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:pn-bond-cannot-be-extremal","label":"rem:pn-bond-cannot-be-extremal","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pn-bond-cannot-be-extremal.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.factors_strict_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.factors_strict_mono","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L227-L233","doc":"**The forced ordering.** With the offsets strictly ordered and `tr₂(σ + d) = z + d`\naffine, the three trace factors are strictly ordered the same way. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.dPN_strict_between","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.dPN_strict_between","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L220-L225","doc":"The `pn` offset lies strictly between the `nn` offset `-h` and the `pp` offset `0`,\nwhenever `0 < h` and `0 < δ < 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.convex_weights_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.convex_weights_sum","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L217-L218","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.dPN_eq_convex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.dPN_eq_convex","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L210-L215","doc":"The `pn` offset written as the convex combination of the `pp` offset `0` and the\n`nn` offset `-h` with weights `1/2 + δ/4` and `1/2 - δ/4`, which sum to `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.L_nn_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.L_nn_eq","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L184-L189","doc":"`L_nn = log q + log(q² + 1)`: the `nn` bond constant in closed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.L_pp_add_L_nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.L_pp_add_L_nn","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L176-L182","doc":"`L_pp + L_nn = 2 log(q + q⁻¹) = 2 log [2]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.L_pn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.L_pn","kind":"def","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L174-L174","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.L_nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.L_nn","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L173-L173","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.L_pp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.L_pp","kind":"def","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L171-L172","doc":"The three bond constants as `-log` of their two-strand factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.neg_log_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.neg_log_prod","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L165-L169","doc":"`-log` of a product of positive factors is the sum of the `-log`s: given the\nfactorisation of the trace over the chain, the canonical `L` is a sum over interfaces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.pn_factor_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.pn_factor_pos","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L155-L163","doc":"The `pn` factor `z + d_pn` is at least the `nn` factor `z - h`, hence positive, for `1 ≤ q`:\n`d_pn = -h/2 + hδ/4 ≥ -h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.deltaPN_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.deltaPN_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L146-L153","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.heckeH_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.heckeH_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L137-L144","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.mirror_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.mirror_pos","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L133-L135","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.markovZ_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.markovZ_pos","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L129-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.markovZ_mul_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.markovZ_mul_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L121-L127","doc":"`tr₂(σ) · tr₂(σ⁻¹) = 1 / [2]_q²`, with `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.markovZ_sub_heckeH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.markovZ_sub_heckeH","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L113-L119","doc":"**The mirror factor.** `tr₂(σ⁻¹) = tr₂(σ - h) = z - h = 1 / (q (q² + 1))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.twoStrandTrace_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.twoStrandTrace_zero","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L109-L111","doc":"`tr₂(σ) = z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.twoStrandTrace_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.twoStrandTrace_eq","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L100-L107","doc":"**The affine law.** `tr₂(σ + d) = z + d`. This is the factor every interface\ngenerator of the canonical word contributes. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:canonical-trace-factorises-over-chain","label":"rem:canonical-trace-factorises-over-chain","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/canonical-trace-factorises-over-chain.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.wPlus_add_wMinus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.wPlus_add_wMinus","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L93-L98","doc":"The two weights sum to one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.wMinus_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.wMinus_eq","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L87-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.wPlus_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.wPlus_eq","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L81-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.qint3_add_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.qint3_add_one","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L76-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.qint3_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.qint3_eq","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L72-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.twoStrandTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.twoStrandTrace","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L69-L70","doc":"Two-strand Markov trace of the letter `σ + d·1`: `σ ↦ q` on `(2)`, `σ ↦ -q⁻¹` on `(1,1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.dPN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.dPN","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L65-L67","doc":"The `pn` offset `d_pn = -h (1 - δ/2) / 2` (`pn_interface_offset`,\n`bring_color_weighted` convention). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.deltaPN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.deltaPN","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L62-L63","doc":"The interface correction `δ = (q - 1)² (1 - q⁻⁴) / 3` of the `pn` offset. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.heckeH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.heckeH","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L59-L60","doc":"The Hecke parameter `h = q - q⁻¹`; the quadratic relation is `σ - σ⁻¹ = h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.markovZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.markovZ","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L56-L57","doc":"The Markov weight `z = q³ / (q² + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.wMinus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.wMinus","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L53-L54","doc":"Wenzl level-2 weight of the column `(1,1)`: `1 / ([3]_q + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.wPlus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.wPlus","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L50-L51","doc":"Wenzl level-2 weight of the row `(2)` in `H₂` under convention D: `[3]_q / ([3]_q + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.qint3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor.qint3","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ChainTraceFactor.lean#L47-L48","doc":"The quantum integer `[3]_q = q² + 1 + q⁻²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}